1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,662
In a city of millions, the hardest part

2
00:00:03,702 --> 00:00:06,795
of the weekend isn't picking a movie.

3
00:00:06,835 --> 00:00:09,505
It's finding someone to go with.

4
00:00:09,545 --> 00:00:12,723
Meet Temenin, the app that finds you a

5
00:00:12,763 --> 00:00:14,755
verified activity buddy.

6
00:00:14,795 --> 00:00:16,872
Vibes click. Plans stick.

7
00:00:17,262 --> 00:00:20,190
This is Nadia. She's new in Jakarta,

8
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:24,560
and this Saturday she wants to catch a
film in Tebet,

9
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:26,951
but nobody she knows is free.

10
00:00:26,991 --> 00:00:30,496
She opens Temenin as an unverified
account.

11
00:00:30,536 --> 00:00:35,113
Notice the board: you can read every
plan's description,

12
00:00:35,153 --> 00:00:40,142
but names, places, and times stay
locked. Verified eyes only.

13
00:00:40,532 --> 00:00:43,563
One quick ID check in the Safety Center,

14
00:00:43,603 --> 00:00:45,713
and the same board opens up.

15
00:00:45,753 --> 00:00:50,243
Names, areas, and times appear, each
with a verified badge.

16
00:00:50,283 --> 00:00:53,084
And this isn't just hidden on screen.

17
00:00:53,124 --> 00:00:56,693
The privacy rule is enforced in the data
layer,

18
00:00:56,733 --> 00:01:00,532
so a display bug can never leak who's
going where.

19
00:01:00,922 --> 00:01:03,148
Now Nadia posts her own plan.

20
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:07,368
She just types one sentence, like she'd
text a friend.

21
00:01:07,408 --> 00:01:11,510
Temenin's concierge turns it into a
structured draft:

22
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:14,636
category, area, budget, even chat level.

23
00:01:14,676 --> 00:01:18,075
Then she sets her House Rules for this
plan:

24
00:01:18,115 --> 00:01:20,810
what's a must, what's just a bonus.

25
00:01:20,850 --> 00:01:26,202
Every plan can have different rules,
because every plan is different.

26
00:01:26,592 --> 00:01:28,658
Here's the part we love most.

27
00:01:28,698 --> 00:01:33,305
Every candidate gets a deterministic
score from five components:

28
00:01:33,345 --> 00:01:38,243
gender preference, shared interests,
energy fit, context, and trust.

29
00:01:38,283 --> 00:01:39,913
Nothing is a black box.

30
00:01:39,953 --> 00:01:44,488
Weaker fits drop down the ranking with
their score in the open,

31
00:01:44,528 --> 00:01:49,280
next to a checklist showing exactly
which of your rules they meet.

32
00:01:49,670 --> 00:01:52,758
Tap a candidate and you get the full
story.

33
00:01:52,798 --> 00:01:57,124
Five score bars, a plain-language reason
written for humans,

34
00:01:57,164 --> 00:01:59,743
three icebreakers to start the chat,

35
00:01:59,783 --> 00:02:03,817
and three public venues picked only from
a curated list.

36
00:02:03,857 --> 00:02:06,000
The app never invents a place.

37
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:10,438
A safety checklist sits right there
before you can reach out.

38
00:02:10,828 --> 00:02:13,685
They chat inside the app, and watch
this:

39
00:02:13,725 --> 00:02:16,724
when Nadia tries to share her phone
number,

40
00:02:16,764 --> 00:02:22,590
the filter holds the message with a gentle reminder to stay in-app until
they meet.

41
00:02:22,630 --> 00:02:26,406
Then both sides tick the safety
checklist and confirm.

42
00:02:26,446 --> 00:02:31,282
Only now, after a two-sided yes, does
the exact meeting point appear.

43
00:02:31,322 --> 00:02:35,028
One tap shares the whole plan with a
trusted contact.

44
00:02:35,418 --> 00:02:40,871
After the movie, Nadia taps home safe,
then leaves stars, quick tags,

45
00:02:40,911 --> 00:02:41,747
and a note.

46
00:02:41,787 --> 00:02:45,488
Her buddy's trust and reliability scores
go up,

47
00:02:45,528 --> 00:02:48,354
so the next plan sticks even better.

48
00:02:48,394 --> 00:02:51,936
That's Temenin: real plans, verified
buddies,

49
00:02:51,976 --> 00:02:54,404
safety built in, not bolted on.

50
00:02:54,444 --> 00:02:59,738
The link to the live demo is in the
description. See you out there.

